---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Privacy policy" description="What Engrebodds collects (very little), why, and your rights." noindex>
  <div class="stack prose" style="max-width:72ch">
    <div>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="draft"><strong>Draft, needs legal review.</strong> This must be checked by a lawyer against the UK GDPR and Nigeria's Data Protection Act 2023 before launch, and again before accounts open.</p>
    </div>
    <section>
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>Engrebodds is operated from the United Kingdom. [Legal name, address and contact to be added.]</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>What we collect today</h2>
      <p>Nothing that identifies you. There are no accounts, no forms and no advertising or tracking cookies.</p>
      <ul class="prose-list">
        <li><strong>Hosting logs.</strong> Our host, Cloudflare, processes your IP address and browser details to deliver pages and protect the site from abuse.</li>
        <li><strong>Visit statistics.</strong> We plan to use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which counts visits without cookies and without identifying you.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Where data is stored</h2>
      <p>Our football data and tips are stored with Supabase in London. Cloudflare serves the site from data centres worldwide.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>When accounts open</h2>
      <p>Premium accounts (planned for August 2027) will need your email address and payment through a Nigerian payment provider. This policy will be updated to say exactly what is collected, why, for how long and who processes it, before any account can be created.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the UK GDPR and the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 you can ask what data we hold about you, have it corrected or deleted, and complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office or the Nigeria Data Protection Commission. [Contact route to be added.]</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
